In article <91Mar1.102038est.2159@ois.db.toronto.edu> jdd@db.toronto.edu (John DiMarco) writes:
>One more problem with Nethack: the ring of conflict is a little too 
>powerful. 
>
>If a player has a ring of conflict, he/she doesn't need to deal with the
>hordes of difficult monsters on the Castle and endgame levels. They all
>start fighting among themselves, resulting in most of them being killed
>off and the ones remaining being severely weakened.

I see no problem here.  If the monsters kill each other off, the
player gets no points for it.  Your score depends an awful lot on the
monsters you kill.  So in the end, the scorefile will show things
fairly, by placing those who used a ring of conflict well below those
who actually killed all the monsters in the castle.  Also, killing
monsters can get you lots of useful items.

